{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1556069-rules-question","id":1556069,"title":"Rules question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-01T14:24:33-08:00","id":1556069,"title":"Rules question","content":"Maybe I am missing something but How does perception work in storypath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25501-nina_blain","name":"nina_blain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T14:00:48-08:00","id":1556103,"title":"","content":"There is no general perception skill. You should sellect a skill based upon the kind of thing the character is observing and or how. If you are examining the site of shootout you might use Ranged, if you are figuring out what is off in a mechanic's shop you might use pilot or technology, and if you are spotting what stands out in a night club you might use culture. If no skill really applies and you are looking for a general attention roll I have used Cunning + Composure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","user":"Slagheap","date":".  spelling error 12-03-2025, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T21:03:34-08:00","id":1556110,"title":"","content":"Searching through the subforums for other Storypath games some time ago, the impression I got was that &quot;generic&quot; action-adventure perception rolls (detecting ambushes/traps/etc.) could springboard off of either Larceny or Survival, depending on the player's/character's aptitudes, or potentially even Enigmas. Larceny, here, extends the knowledge of where to hide or how to conceal something into awareness of where and how others could attempt the same. Survival, alternatively, leans into a more &quot;typical&quot; approach to RPG perception, being exceptionally in-tune with subtle sensory cues in one's environment, whether it's the faint draft of an cave exit or a shifting curtain, or the subtle smells of oncoming rain or a lurking predator. Enigmas, in turn, as the centerpiece of investigation, could be leveraged for a &quot;Sherlock Scan&quot; approach, assessing scenery cues from a more academic or deductive perspective.<br /> <br /> Honestly, weird as it may sound, I <i>like</i> the lack of a &quot;Perception&quot; or &quot;Awareness&quot; skill. It almost feels <i>obligatory</i> in many systems that do have one, even <i>mandatory</i> in a &quot;take this to not die&quot; sense - where with what I found searching the other Storypath subforums, it feels less about &quot;Is my character <i>capable</i> of recognizing potential danger?&quot; and more about &quot;<i>H</i><i>ow</i> does my character recognize potential danger?&quot; - and from there, &quot;How might that knowledge or past experience color my character's reaction?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3388-r0gue_rob0t","name":"r0gue_rob0t","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T08:24:59-08:00","id":1556145,"title":"","content":"thanks guys that does help me i was a bit stuck as im used to the 'Obligatory&quot; perceptions in other games but this is a better way to do it with meaning. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25501-nina_blain","name":"nina_blain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T10:50:34-08:00","id":1556798,"title":"","content":"Assuming this is where you ask for questions about rules.<br /> <br /> There is a bit that kinda confuses me about the book. Sometimes the book will ask you an action for certain spells or power (such as Spell Mimicry or the Bombardment spell) where they only say the Skill used, such as &quot;an Esoterica action&quot; or &quot;an Empathy action&quot;. There are no mention of the Attribute you are supposed to roll with it. Does it mean you roll the skill alone for those actions, or that you must decide which Attribute is used based on the guidelines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}